-- Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (WA), with the Uniform Law (WA), Admission Rules and General Rules, costs -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_legal-profession-uniform-law-application-act-2022_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- d038 (4 Mar 2029): Daniel acts for a client in an arbitration under a conditional costs agreement with a 25% uplift. The
-- life gives only that; the agreement's other terms (written, signed, a 5-business-day cooling-off, the uplift's basis and
-- estimate, the firm's belief in success) and the client's first instructions on 1 Feb 2029 are HYPOTHETICAL.

§ `fixtures`

`Daniel's arbitration agreement with a 25% uplift` MEANS `My conditional costs agreement` WITH
    `written and in plain language` IS TRUE
    `it sets out what counts as a successful outcome` IS TRUE
    `signed by the client` IS TRUE
    `it states the client was told of the right to independent advice` IS TRUE
    `cooling-off period in clear business days` IS 5
    `made between law practices only` IS FALSE
    `it provides for an uplift fee` IS TRUE
    `uplift as a percentage of legal costs excluding disbursements` IS 25
    `my firm reasonably believes success is reasonably likely` IS TRUE
    `it identifies the basis of the uplift and estimates it` IS TRUE
    `fees calculated by reference to the award, settlement or property recovered` IS FALSE
    `that calculation adopts an applicable costs determination` IS FALSE

