§ `Uniform Law Sch 4 cl 18 -- d038: Part 4.3 governs a matter first instructed in 2029`

#ASSERT `Does Part 4.3 govern my fees in this matter` (Date 1 2 2029)

§ `Uniform Law ss 6, 181(7) -- d038: may an arbitration have a conditional costs agreement`

#ASSERT `May the costs agreement be conditional for this matter` `an arbitration`
#ASSERT NOT `May the costs agreement be conditional for this matter` `criminal proceedings`

-- The fork: an arbitration with no court application in view, on each reading of "tribunal".
#ASSERT NOT `Is my matter a litigious matter` `an arbitration` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my matter a litigious matter` `an arbitration` TRUE FALSE

§ `Uniform Law ss 180-183 -- d038: the agreement and its 25% uplift`

#ASSERT `Does the agreement meet the form requirements` `Daniel's arbitration agreement with a 25% uplift`
#ASSERT NOT `Does the agreement meet the form requirements` `the same with a 3-day cooling-off period`

-- 25% in a litigious matter with a reasonable belief: allowed. 30% in a litigious matter: not. 30% if the arbitration is not a
-- litigious matter: s 182(2) does not apply, so no cap.
#ASSERT `Is the uplift fee allowed` `Daniel's arbitration agreement with a 25% uplift` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is the uplift fee allowed` `the same with a 30% uplift` TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the uplift fee allowed` `the same with a 30% uplift` FALSE

#ASSERT `Is the agreement a prohibited contingency fee` `the same with fees as 20% of the award`

§ `Uniform Law ss 184, 185 -- d038: is it valid, and what can be recovered`

#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `an arbitration` FALSE FALSE `Daniel's arbitration agreement with a 25% uplift` EQUALS `valid: it may be enforced like any other contract (s 184)`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `an arbitration` TRUE FALSE `the same with a 30% uplift` EQUALS `void: the uplift breaches s 182, so no part of the uplift fee is recoverable (s 185(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `an arbitration` FALSE FALSE `the same with fees as 20% of the award` EQUALS `void: a contingency fee, so my firm may recover nothing for the services and must repay what it received (s 185(4))`

#ASSERT `What is the most my firm can be ordered to pay`  EQUALS 100

#ASSERT `Can the breach be a conduct matter against me` TRUE TRUE

§ `Application Act ss 3, 132-134 -- d038: may a WA costs determination cover the arbitration (the fork)`

#ASSERT `May a costs determination cover my work` `an arbitrator` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May a costs determination cover my work` `an arbitrator` FALSE TRUE FALSE

§ `Application Act ss 140, 141, 143, 149, 151`

#ASSERT `From when does the determination govern my fees` (Date 1 3 2029) TRUE (Date 1 4 2029) EQUALS (Date 1 4 2029)

-- d038: Daniel's valid conditional costs agreement governs instead of any determination; a void one would not.
#ASSERT NOT `Does a costs determination govern my fees` `a determination and Daniel's valid agreement`
#ASSERT `Does a costs determination govern my fees` `a determination and a void agreement`

#ASSERT `Has my firm breached section 143` TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `Can I still apply for review of the assessment` (Date 1 3 2029) (Date 29 3 2029)

#ASSERT `How much must my firm repay` 12000 10000 EQUALS 2000

